  "name": "Question 10",
  "problem": "Let $u=[\\begin{aligned}k \\\\ 1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]$ and $v=[\\begin{aligned}3k \\\\ -6 \\\\ k \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]$ be vectors such that  $u\u22a5v.$ Find the value of $k.$",
  "worked_solution": "Since $u$ and $v$ are orthogonal vectors, we have that their dot product is equal to zero.\nFirst, let's calculate the dot product in terms of $k$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u\\cdot v & ={u}_{1}\\cdot {v}_{1}+{u}_{2}\\cdot {v}_{2}+{u}_{3}\\cdot {v}_{3}+{u}_{4}\\cdot {v}_{4} \\\\  & =k\\cdot 3k+1\\cdot (-6)+3\\cdot k+(-2)\\cdot 0 \\\\  & =3{k}^{2}-6+3k+0 \\\\  & =3({k}^{2}+k-2)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the dot product to zero, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3({k}^{2}+k-2) & =0 \\\\ 3(k+2)(k-1) & =0 \\\\ k & =-2,1.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
